  "name": "IGM BY IMMUNOTURBIDMETRY",
  "code": "1119",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"89\" data-end=\"227\">\n<p data-start=\"91\" data-end=\"227\">Immunoglobulin M (IgM) is the first antibody produced in response to an infection and plays a key role in the primary immune response.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"228\" data-end=\"340\">\n<p data-start=\"230\" data-end=\"340\">It is mainly present in the blood and lymphatic fluid and provides early defense against invading pathogens.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"341\" data-end=\"470\">\n<p data-start=\"343\" data-end=\"470\">Measurement of IgM levels helps in assessing acute or recent infections, immune system disorders, and plasma cell dyscrasias.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"471\" data-end=\"608\">\n<p data-start=\"473\" data-end=\"608\">It is useful in diagnosing conditions like Waldenstr&ouml;m&rsquo;s macroglobulinemia, various types of immunodeficiency, and autoimmune diseases.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>IgM Level</th>\n<th>Possible Clinical Indications</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Elevated</td>\n<td>Recent or acute infections (viral, bacterial), autoimmune diseases (e.g., lupus, rheumatoid arthritis), Waldenstr&ouml;m&rsquo;s macroglobulinemia, monoclonal gammopathies, chronic liver diseases (e.g., primary biliary cholangitis)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n<td>Primary immunodeficiency syndromes (e.g., selective IgM deficiency, common variable immunodeficiency), protein-losing conditions, leukemia, chemotherapy or immunosuppressive therapy</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
